1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,529
Welcome to RecruitIQ, an AI recruitment platform built for recruitment

2
00:00:05,549 --> 00:00:06,572
agencies.

3
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:11,683
Agencies hire on behalf of their client companies.

4
00:00:12,252 --> 00:00:15,994
Screening hundreds of resumes and scheduling first-round interviews

5
00:00:16,014 --> 00:00:20,444
by hand is slow, and good candidates are often lost along the way.

6
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:24,727
RecruitIQ automates that first round.

7
00:00:25,296 --> 00:00:27,949
The agency shares one private link.

8
00:00:28,495 --> 00:00:32,188
Candidates upload a resume, see their match instantly,

9
00:00:32,208 --> 00:00:35,840
verify their email, and take an AI voice interview,

10
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,359
while recruiters simply review the reports and decide.

11
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,176
The platform is run by a Portal Admin,

12
00:00:43,196 --> 00:00:45,726
who onboards recruitment agencies.

13
00:00:46,259 --> 00:00:50,369
There is no public sign-up, and the admin can suspend or reactivate

14
00:00:50,389 --> 00:00:51,681
any agency.

15
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:55,825
Let's sign in as Nexora Talent Partners,

16
00:00:55,845 --> 00:00:57,321
a demo agency.

17
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:04,418
The dashboard shows what needs attention today:

18
00:01:04,438 --> 00:01:07,555
open jobs, total candidates, interviews,

19
00:01:07,575 --> 00:01:09,628
and the average interview score.

20
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:18,005
The candidate pipeline shows how many applicants are at each stage,

21
00:01:18,025 --> 00:01:21,963
and Recent AI Interviews lists every completed interview,

22
00:01:21,983 --> 00:01:25,394
with its overall, technical and communication scores,

23
00:01:25,414 --> 00:01:27,320
and a security status.

24
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:32,968
From the sidebar, the agency also manages its client companies,

25
00:01:32,988 --> 00:01:35,578
with their departments and HR contacts,

26
00:01:35,598 --> 00:01:37,649
and its own team of recruiters,

27
00:01:37,669 --> 00:01:39,672
each with their own permissions.

28
00:01:43,790 --> 00:01:48,646
Now let's post a new job. The recruiter only needs a title and a

29
00:01:48,666 --> 00:01:51,381
description, written in plain language.

30
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:59,025
This role is for the agency's client,

31
00:01:59,045 --> 00:02:02,762
Finlytics Software, and is linked to their HR contact,

32
00:02:02,782 --> 00:02:05,484
who will later receive the best candidates.

33
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:10,620
Clicking Auto-fill details from description sends the text to the

34
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:14,335
AI, which extracts the structured job details.

35
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,217
Within seconds, work mode, openings,

36
00:02:18,237 --> 00:02:21,036
experience, salary, notice period,

37
00:02:21,056 --> 00:02:23,842
location, required and preferred skills,

38
00:02:23,862 --> 00:02:26,564
languages and education are filled in.

39
00:02:27,121 --> 00:02:29,859
Each one is marked as filled from the description,

40
00:02:29,879 --> 00:02:33,046
so the recruiter can review and correct anything.

41
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:37,431
One click on Publish job, and the role is live,

42
00:02:37,451 --> 00:02:39,332
with its own shareable link.

43
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:46,625
Every job has an Interviews and setup page.

44
00:02:47,170 --> 00:02:49,822
Here the recruiter copies the candidate link,

45
00:02:49,842 --> 00:02:53,277
for this job or for all of the agency's open roles,

46
00:02:53,297 --> 00:02:56,048
and can optionally set an interview window.

47
00:02:57,230 --> 00:03:00,188
The AI interviewer is fully configurable:

48
00:03:00,208 --> 00:03:03,717
its name and title, voice, the number of questions,

49
00:03:03,737 --> 00:03:06,182
and the time allowed for each answer.

50
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:11,641
Recruiters can add custom questions the AI must always ask,

51
00:03:11,661 --> 00:03:15,258
skills it must cover, and evaluation criteria.

52
00:03:15,815 --> 00:03:19,839
The interview report will later mark each criterion as met,

53
00:03:19,859 --> 00:03:22,144
partly met, or not met.

54
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:27,136
On the Applications page, the recruiter sets the minimum resume

55
00:03:27,156 --> 00:03:29,109
match needed to get an interview,

56
00:03:29,129 --> 00:03:31,929
and how the final score is calculated.

57
00:03:32,461 --> 00:03:36,657
Here, it is thirty percent CV match and seventy percent interview,

58
00:03:36,677 --> 00:03:39,207
with a qualifying threshold of seventy.

59
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:43,012
Now let's switch to the candidate's side.

60
00:03:43,569 --> 00:03:46,234
A candidate opens the agency's link.

61
00:03:46,779 --> 00:03:49,124
There is no login and no account,

62
00:03:49,144 --> 00:03:51,491
just the agency's open roles.

63
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:57,692
Not sure which role fits? The candidate uploads a resume once,

64
00:03:57,712 --> 00:04:00,561
and RecruitIQ finds the matching roles.

65
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:10,310
The AI reads the resume and scores it against the agency's best-fitting

66
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:14,380
open roles, checking skills, experience and education.

67
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:19,772
Kavya, a full-stack developer, is a one hundred percent match for

68
00:04:19,792 --> 00:04:24,492
MERN Stack Developer, and also qualifies for two other roles.

69
00:04:25,049 --> 00:04:28,436
Roles below the minimum score are marked Not eligible,

70
00:04:28,456 --> 00:04:30,190
and cannot be selected.

71
00:04:31,370 --> 00:04:34,979
She applies for the MERN Stack Developer role.

72
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:42,994
To make sure only the resume's real owner can apply,

73
00:04:43,014 --> 00:04:47,186
a six-digit code is sent to the email address written on the resume.

74
00:04:47,731 --> 00:04:50,604
The candidate never types an email address.

75
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:54,153
She enters the code from her email,

76
00:04:57,470 --> 00:05:00,344
and her interview link is ready immediately.

77
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:03,860
No shortlisting delay, and no scheduling.

78
00:05:04,405 --> 00:05:07,438
The same link is also sent to her by email.

79
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,937
What if a resume doesn't fit? Here,

80
00:05:11,957 --> 00:05:15,578
a customer support resume is uploaded for the same job.

81
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:19,002
Its match is only nineteen percent,

82
00:05:19,022 --> 00:05:21,109
below the requirement for this job,

83
00:05:21,129 --> 00:05:23,317
so the candidate cannot continue.

84
00:05:23,861 --> 00:05:28,438
No application is created, so recruiters never have to screen it.

85
00:05:29,590 --> 00:05:34,201
Back to Kavya. Her interview link opens a short checklist:

86
00:05:34,221 --> 00:05:38,651
camera on, a quiet room, and about twenty to thirty minutes.

87
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:43,525
In the interview room, she checks her camera and microphone,

88
00:05:43,545 --> 00:05:47,864
and joins. The camera is used for presence only.

89
00:05:48,422 --> 00:05:50,511
Nothing is recorded or stored.

90
00:05:55,850 --> 00:06:00,663
Ananya (AI interviewer): Hi Kavya, I'm Ananya, Senior Technical Recruiter at Nexora Talent

91
00:06:00,683 --> 00:06:04,471
Partners. Thanks for joining â€” let's get started.

92
00:06:04,491 --> 00:06:10,210
Could you briefly introduce yourself and walk me through your background?

93
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:15,490
The AI interviewer, Ananya, greets her by name and asks each question

94
00:06:15,510 --> 00:06:19,020
aloud. Kavya answers by speaking.

95
00:06:19,565 --> 00:06:22,266
Her answer is transcribed live on screen,

96
00:06:22,286 --> 00:06:24,865
and she presses Send when she is done.

97
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:29,274
Each question is generated from the job description,

98
00:06:29,294 --> 00:06:32,156
her resume, and her earlier answers.

99
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:35,425
The number of questions is fixed by the system,

100
00:06:35,445 --> 00:06:38,833
and the difficulty adapts to how well she answers.

101
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,088
When an answer needs more depth,

102
00:06:42,108 --> 00:06:44,563
the AI asks a follow-up question,

103
00:06:44,583 --> 00:06:45,913
like this one.

104
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:50,295
Throughout the interview, events like tab switches,

105
00:06:50,315 --> 00:06:54,278
camera and microphone changes, and connection drops are logged for

106
00:06:54,298 --> 00:06:55,860
a security audit.

107
00:06:57,010 --> 00:07:00,349
At the end, Kavya can ask her own questions.

108
00:07:00,894 --> 00:07:05,188
The AI answers using only the job and company information,

109
00:07:05,208 --> 00:07:07,186
and then closes the interview.

110
00:07:08,330 --> 00:07:13,040
As soon as the interview ends, RecruitIQ writes the report and calculates

111
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:16,986
the final score. Back on the agency side,

112
00:07:17,005 --> 00:07:19,314
Kavya now ranks first for this job,

113
00:07:19,334 --> 00:07:22,990
with her resume match, interview score and final score,

114
00:07:23,010 --> 00:07:26,227
and she has been automatically marked Qualified.

115
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:35,281
Here is her interview report: an overall score of ninety,

116
00:07:35,301 --> 00:07:38,111
with separate technical and communication scores,

117
00:07:38,131 --> 00:07:42,194
a written summary, strengths, and areas for improvement.

118
00:07:48,330 --> 00:07:52,477
Each of the recruiter's evaluation criteria is assessed as met,

119
00:07:52,497 --> 00:07:56,559
partly met, or not met, with evidence from the interview.

120
00:07:57,790 --> 00:08:01,667
The full transcript is kept, with a score for every answer,

121
00:08:01,687 --> 00:08:05,075
along with the interview and security event log.

122
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:11,774
Her candidate page brings it all together:

123
00:08:11,794 --> 00:08:15,536
a CV match of one hundred, an interview score of ninety,

124
00:08:15,556 --> 00:08:17,754
and a final score of ninety-three,

125
00:08:17,774 --> 00:08:21,076
with matched and missing skills and the AI's reasoning.

126
00:08:21,621 --> 00:08:25,155
For fairness, the AI never sees a candidate's name,

127
00:08:25,175 --> 00:08:28,343
gender or other personal details when scoring.

128
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:35,938
Kavya is a strong fit, so the recruiter clicks Submit to company.

129
00:08:36,495 --> 00:08:39,871
The preview shows exactly what the client will receive.

130
00:08:40,417 --> 00:08:43,620
The recruiter confirms Finlytics' HR contact,

131
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:46,305
adds a note, and sends the package.

132
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:55,280
The client's HR contact signs in to the Company HR portal,

133
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:58,333
and sees only the candidates submitted to them.

134
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:06,287
They can review the scores, the interview evaluation,

135
00:09:06,307 --> 00:09:08,836
the hiring criteria and each question,

136
00:09:08,856 --> 00:09:11,618
view or download the CV, and if needed,

137
00:09:11,638 --> 00:09:13,972
request a second-round interview.

138
00:09:22,130 --> 00:09:27,024
Back on the agency side, Kavya's status is now Submitted to Company,

139
00:09:27,044 --> 00:09:30,284
and the submission history records who received the package,

140
00:09:30,304 --> 00:09:31,829
and when it was viewed.

141
00:09:33,290 --> 00:09:38,612
So that's RecruitIQ. One private link replaces manual first-round

142
00:09:38,632 --> 00:09:43,453
screening. AI resume matching filters applicants instantly,

143
00:09:43,473 --> 00:09:47,203
verified candidates take an adaptive AI voice interview,

144
00:09:47,223 --> 00:09:51,382
and recruiters get clear, evidence-based reports to submit the best

145
00:09:51,402 --> 00:09:53,319
candidates to their clients.

146
00:09:54,760 --> 00:10:00,500
RecruitIQ. Hire faster with AI resume matching and voice interviews.

